# Octon Mini Long-Running Work

This optional package governs one external worker performing bounded,
long-running work under an existing `TASK-####`. It does not host a model,
grant permission, create task scope, or replace transactions, project-check
evidence, work completion, events, decisions, or the Continuation Contract.

The package is installed disabled. After a separate accepted project decision,
create its project-owned adoption record through the package command. Package
installation, adoption, run creation, validation, and completion remain
separate facts.

Use the generated dispatcher:

```text
./octon work run --help
./octon work run context --task-id TASK-0001 --max-bytes 65536 --json
./octon work run start --task-id TASK-0001 --limits limits.json --allow-path src
./octon work run status --json
./octon work run resume --json
```

On Windows, invoke the same launcher as `python -B octon` or `py -3 -B octon`.

Run records live under `.agent/work-runs/`, outside the immutable
installed-payload digest. Only marker-backed checkpoints are
committed. Read-only commands execute no project hooks and write no files.
Elapsed limits use the local clock; externally reported token and cost totals
are optional, nonnegative, monotonic values and remain unknown when unavailable.

External work still uses the existing transaction or `work.finish` boundary.
An ambiguous external outcome stops for reconciliation and is never replayed.

See the source specification at `docs/LONG_RUNNING_WORK.md` in the Octon Mini
source bundle. That source document and this package create no project
authority or readiness claim.
